module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_ordered_choice_reparses_a_committed_subexpression

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data an_ordered_choice_reparses_a_committed_subexpression: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_ordered_choice_reparses_a_committed_subexpression" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an ordered grammar Choice re-parses a sub-expression that an earlier alternative already parsed in full. The alternatives are tried in declared order; an alternative that parses a complete nested body before the enclosing choice can fail leaves that body to be parsed again by every later alternative. Nothing records that position and production were already attempted, so the recomputation is invisible and the cost of one construct becomes multiplicative in its own nesting depth. The class is named for the RE-PARSE rather than for backtracking, because backtracking is admissible and the defect is the absent memo of what a committed alternative established.",

    "THE DISTINGUISHING OBSERVATION, and it is a two-shape discriminator rather than a slope. Hold nesting depth, file size class, binary and command constant and vary only WHICH construct nests. Nested function literals in argument position cost 0.2, 0.6, 3.2 and 24.1 seconds at depths 1 through 4 -- a factor of about 7.5 per level. Nested match arms at the same depths are FLAT at 0.2 seconds. A cost that tracked tree size, spine depth or a walker's re-entry would move in both shapes. It moves in one, which locates the defect in the production rather than in the traversal.",

    "THE MECHANISM, READ FROM THE GRAMMAR AND NOT INFERRED FROM THE NUMBER. `v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_grammar_expr_expr` orders the expression alternatives match, if, loop, fn_literal, block, arrow_lambda, binary. `match_expr` is FIRST, so a match commits on its keyword and no later alternative re-reads its body -- which is exactly why the match shape is flat and is the control that makes this reading falsifiable. `dag_grammar_fn_literal_expr` sits FOURTH and parses a full `dag_production_fn_body` before the enclosing choice can fail, so a later alternative re-parses that body, and each nesting level re-parses every level inside it once per surviving alternative.",

    "THE RESOURCE SHAPE RULES OUT THE COMPETING EXPLANATIONS. At depth 3 wall is 3.07s against cpu_user 3.06s; at depth 4 wall is 23.86s against cpu_user 23.82s; maxrss is 11264 kB at BOTH depths. CPU equals wall, so it is not contention or IO; resident memory does not move with depth, so it is not allocation growth, tree retention or a sharing failure. It is recomputation.",

    "RECEIPT, 2026-09-25, reducing the #12210 native cost blocker. Declaration-level reduction of `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` under isolated census: 333 blocks at 348s, prefix 187 at 10s, prefix 188 at 84s, and the one added declaration `body_lower_comma_list_repeat_items` ALONE at 45.3s in 140 lines while its neighbour alone is 0.2s. That declaration nests four `bind_outcome(o:, f: fn(...) {...})` closures. Its recursive and non-recursive variants time identically at 0.5 and 2.8 against 0.5 and 2.7 seconds for depths 1 and 2, which removed recursion as the variable. Import-free fixtures of 9 to 17 lines reproduce the whole curve, so no part of this needs the closure present.",

    "THE INTERPRETED-VERSUS-EMITTED COMPARISON THIS ROW CARRIED IS RETRACTED: IT COMPARED TWO REVISIONS, NOT TWO REALIZATIONS. The emitted measurements come from a binary built from a head containing gunbc#12210; the interpreted runs were executed on a branch where `git merge-base --is-ancestor` reports that #12210 is NOT an ancestor. So the earlier conclusion that only the emitted realization exhibits the curve, and that the defect sits at the emitted-realization boundary, is withdrawn as unestablished. What made the confound visible is that a parse-AND-normalize probe over the same nested-closure source returns exit=1 on the non-#12210 branch: normalize REFUSES a function value there, so the cheap side of the comparison is cheap because it REFUSES rather than because it reuses. THE REFUSAL IS CLOSURE-SPECIFIC AND CONTROLLED: on the same branch, same probe and same composition, a braced body carrying NO closure normalizes successfully at 189.7s exit=0, while the nested-closure source refuses at 201.7s exit=1. So the interpreted column was not measuring reuse of the expensive work; it was measuring the absence of the work, behind exactly the wall #12210 removes. THE CONSEQUENCE RUNS AGAINST WHAT THIS ROW ORIGINALLY PUBLISHED: the function-value handling that #12210 introduces is the proximate suspect for the cost, not a pre-existing parser defect beneath it, and the earlier statement that the semantics of that change are exonerated is withdrawn.",

    "THE MODELLED MEMO IS EXCLUDED AS THE MECHANISM, and this is a measurement rather than a reading. An arm-entry trace records ZERO dispatches of the interpreter's parse_table_lookup special. The model calls that function unconditionally inside parse_nonterminal_memoized_core, immediately after grammar_lookup_production_indexed succeeds, so zero dispatches means the memoized core is never reached and the prepared-plan path does not route through it. Both realizations execute the same declarations, so the modelled memo is on NEITHER path. Bypassing the special outright leaves every depth flat -- 201.4s, 191.4s, 189.3s, 199.9s and 202.7s at depths 1, 2, 3, 5 and 6, all exit=0 -- which is what a special that never fires predicts. An earlier receipt attributing the interpreter's flatness to the privileged ctx.parse_table_memo provider is withdrawn: that provider exists in code and does not fire here.",

    "WHAT SURVIVES IS MEASURED INSIDE ONE BINARY WITH ONE COMMAND, which is why no revision or realization baseline enters it. Holding depth, file size class, binary and command constant and varying only WHICH CONSTRUCT NESTS: nested function literals cost 0.2s, 0.6s, 3.2s and 24.1s at depths 1 to 4 while nested match arms stay FLAT at 0.2s -- a 120-fold separation at equal depth. CPU equals wall and maxrss is unchanged at 11264 kB across depths, so it is recomputation rather than allocation growth, contention or IO. Node count and spine depth cannot separate those two columns, so both remain retired as the causal variable. `census` composes tokenize, parse and normalize and does not resolve.",

    "THE STAGE IS OPEN, AND THE GRAMMAR ACCOUNT BELOW IS A CANDIDATE RATHER THAN A FINDING. A tokenize-and-parse-only probe is depth-flat, but its SENSITIVITY FLOOR is about 20 seconds: a no-parse control costs 182.5s against parse runs of 182.7s to 204.2s, so any parse cost below roughly 20 seconds is undetectable by it. Because census also normalizes, and normalize refuses on the branch where the flat readings were taken, PARSE IS NOT ESTABLISHED AS THE EXPENSIVE STAGE. The ordering argument stated below remains a mechanism fitted to a real curve on a revision that was not isolated. THE CONTROL THAT CLOSES BOTH QUESTIONS is one emitted build with #12210 against the same build with it reverted, over the two tiny fixtures.",

    "WHAT THIS RECEIPT DOES NOT ESTABLISH. The v1 seed front end reports compile.frontend done in 0ms at every one of these depths, which is a fact about v1 against v2 and is not evidence about either v2 realization. Isolated census also has none of the subject file's imports, so this class explains the PARSE cost and makes no claim about the route's zero-split-row behaviour. And the emitted measurements come from ONE preserved experimental binary built 2026-09-25 05:09; the mechanism above is read from current source, but no second emitted build has reproduced the curve, so realization and revision are not fully separated by this evidence.",


    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, and only by a human noticing a route did not finish. The invalid state is fully writable -- any authored nesting of a non-first alternative expresses it -- and nothing bounds a production's re-parse of a position it already attempted.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED. Production and token position are both available where the choice is taken, so a parse that attempts a given production at a given position at most once is derivable from the prepared grammar rather than validated after the fact, and DESIGN section 4's bounded forward execution is the contract it would restore. It is not structurally IMPOSSIBLE while an ordered Choice may re-enter a production at a position it has already attempted.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY, AND IT IS TWO CAPABILITIES BECAUSE THE FALSIFICATION SPLIT IT. FIRST, AND PROXIMATE: the emitted realization preserves the reuse the modelled memo expresses, so that parse cost over one source is the same order in the emitted binary as in the interpreter -- a realization that does not preserve modelled behaviour is a differentiating-claim failure in DESIGN section 4b, and parity over this depth ladder is its discriminator. Naming only the prepared plan here would have been a trigger naming less than the capability it restores: the plan would be built while the emitted realization stayed free to lose reuse at the next production that demands it. SECOND, AND DEEPER: one prepared plan per authored Choice, under which attempting a production at a token position at most once is a property of the plan rather than of the input, so the demand is REMOVED rather than made cheap -- DESIGN section 6b specimen B1, gunbc#11422. The two are ordered, not alternatives: parity without the plan leaves an avoidable recurrence merely memoized, and the plan without parity leaves every other emitted reuse unguarded. WHAT RETIRES NEITHER: widening the memo at the site where the cost was measured, reordering the alternatives so fn_literal commits earlier, which only moves which construct pays, and FLATTENING THE AUTHORED NESTING, which lowers the number while leaving both capabilities absent -- DESIGN section 5's workaround.",


    "WHAT IS EXPLICITLY NOT THIS CLASS: `body_producer_work_is_not_bounded_by_its_declared_input` is the adjacent row and is about a PRODUCER's work tracking a population it does not own. This row is about a PARSE re-establishing a fact an earlier alternative already established. The separating experiment that row names ran here, and its answer was neither of that row's two candidates -- not node count and not spine depth, but which construct nests -- so a specimen attributed to that row on census cost alone should be re-read against this one."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
